{"protocol":{"major":0,"minor":1},"worker_version":"0.0.0-dev.f723212d7267","supervisor_id":"7dea7829-7003-480f-945d-802edb6b693b","supervisor_epoch":"5cb11cec-b59f-4abd-8db8-4e7a45a10ef3","pi_version":"1.5.2","capabilities":["history.jsonl","interrupt_marker","command_stamp","image_attachments"],"limits":{"request_body_bytes":262144,"attachment_max_bytes":2097152,"attachments_per_message":4,"attachments_total_bytes":8388608,"event_frame_bytes":1048576,"journal_max_bytes":33554432,"journal_control_reserve_bytes":1048576,"ordinary_receipts_max":4096,"receipt_retention_min_seconds":3600,"receipt_expired_ids_max":16384,"history_max_bytes":16777216,"history_line_max_bytes":67108864,"blob_max_bytes":16777216,"inventory_probes_max":4},"named_limits":["Private sockets and bearer grants do not isolate hostile code running as the same OS user, including project extensions.","The worker cannot read the peer credentials of a Unix-socket client; its boundary is file modes plus the bearer grant.","A journal on a bring-your-own machine dies with the machine.","Receipts are retained within the advertised limits; an evicted receipt reads as receipt_expired (unknown) while its id is among the most recent receipt_expired_ids_max evicted ids. After that its command still never runs again: an id the worker may have forgotten (a UUIDv7 command_id not issued after the newest forgotten one, or any other id once one such was forgotten) is refused command_id_beyond_retention (no_effect), so callers mint UUIDv7 command ids.","Linux results are not macOS results.","Each worker runs in its own cgroup v2 cleanup domain, which is cleanup, not isolation: hostile code running as the same user can still signal or escape it, and work a tool hands to another daemon (tmux, systemd-run --user, Docker) leaves it.","A sandboxed typed child (launch_spec filesystem bwrap) can write only its root, its cwd, and, when that root is a Git linked worktree, the Git state the next limit names. It shares the network, and its environment allowlist (model API keys included) and any credential store staged read-only in its root are readable inside it. files.read reads only a sandboxed worker root, inside explicit roots, with no symlink, hidden or traversal component, UTF-8 and at most 1 MiB.","When a sandboxed child's root is a Git linked worktree, it can write the worktree admin dir (index, its own reflog, a detached HEAD), the repository object store, which is shared (it can add or remove objects other checkouts use), and, with a symbolic HEAD, its own branch namespace refs/heads/<ns>/ with that namespace's reflogs. The gitfile, gitdir, commondir, a symbolic HEAD, the repository config, packed-refs, every other ref and reflog, and alternates are read-only; the repository hooks and other worktrees' admin dirs are not mounted. An ordinary checkout root, and a linked worktree whose repository lies inside its root or contains it, are refused.","A sandboxed child of a parent whose cwd holds a pi profile (.piw-agent) gets a copy of that profile in its root's .piw-agent, credential stores included, so the child can read everything the parent's profile holds. Links are copied as links and never followed; FIFOs, sockets and devices refuse; the copy is at most 10,000 entries, 256 MiB and depth 32. Each node_modules tree in it (at most 64) is not copied but bound read-only from the parent's profile, so the child sees later changes the parent makes there. A staging failure after the child's .piw-agent was created is outcome_unknown and fences the parent.","Cleanup profile: cgroup_v2_user_delegation: cgroup.kill, populated 0, removed; cleanup, not isolation from same-user code."]}
